---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { bountyRules, insiderRules, money, rulesVersion, shape, site } from '../config/site';
---

<Base title="Rules" description="The rules of the hackathon, in plain words.">
  <h1 class="page-title">The rules, in plain words.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    This is version {rulesVersion}. The rules are published here, and any change to them
    is listed with its date at the bottom of this page.
  </p>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top:16px">Using this site and taking part is also covered by the <a class="link" href="/terms">terms</a>.</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What you build</h2>
    <p>The free, open-source version of something people would otherwise pay for. One feature of a big product is a fair scope.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Open source under an OSI-approved licence, in a public repo.</li>
      <li>No payments, paywalls or paid tiers during the hackathon.</li>
      <li>It has to run: a live link, or install steps the panel can follow.</li>
      <li>An alternative, not a copy. No copied code, assets or branding from the product you are replacing.</li>
      <li>You may start fresh or fork an existing open-source project. If you fork, say what you added.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>When</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>{shape.when}</li>
      <li>Building lasts {site.shape.buildDays} days. Submissions close when they end.</li>
      <li>Builders then vote for {site.shape.votingDays} days. Winners are announced the day after voting closes.</li>
      <li>The dates will be posted here before building starts.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Who can enter</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A GitHub or GitLab account at least {site.eligibility.minAccountAgeDays} days old.</li>
      <li>At least {site.eligibility.minContributions12mo} contributions shown on your profile for the last 12 months.</li>
      <li>One entry per person. Teams enter through a GitHub organization.</li>
      <li>Every entry is submitted as a public GitHub repository. If you work on GitLab, set up a push mirror to GitHub, which GitLab does for you on every push.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Who wins</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Everyone who submits an eligible entry gets three votes for three different projects, not their own.</li>
      <li>Every ballot is published.</li>
      <li>Prizes are shares of the pool: 30%, 18%, 12%, five prizes of 6%, and 10% for Community Choice.</li>
      <li>Community Choice is decided by a wider vote, open to any GitHub or GitLab account that passes the same two checks, one vote each.</li>
      <li>Sponsors get no vote on any prize. Organizers and review panel members get no vote on the main prizes.</li>
      <li>If a winner cannot be paid, their share goes to the next place.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Organizers and the review panel</h2>
    <ul>
      {insiderRules.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <h2>Sponsor bounties</h2>
    <p>A bounty is money a sponsor puts up for the best entry that does one specific thing. It is won on top of any main prize. Bounties are listed on this site as sponsors commit them.</p>
    <ul>
      {bountyRules.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <h2>The money</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>{money.full}</li>
      <li>Every contribution and every payout is public.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Cheating</h2>
    <p>A named volunteer panel reviews flagged entries and the top ten. It can disqualify only for a written rule, publishes its reasoning, and cannot rank anyone. A disqualified builder has 72 hours to appeal in public. A panel member takes no part in a decision about their own entry. The panel's members are named on this site before building starts.</p>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>{site.rules.date}: version {site.rules.version} published.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</Base>
